    'You need Acrobat Sign: certified, legally attributable e-signature requests with identity checks and audit reports.',
    'You already use Acrobat Pro on the desktop and want the online tools to hand files to it, or need its preflight and print-production features.',
    'You want your documents stored in Adobe cloud storage and available across devices and Adobe apps.',
    'You rely on Adobe’s enterprise controls — organisation accounts, retention policies and compliance attestations.',
  ]}
  faqs={[
    { question: 'Do I need an Adobe account to use HatePDF?', answer: 'No account of any kind. Adobe’s online tools require signing in to save or share results; HatePDF saves the result straight from your browser to your device.' },
    { question: 'Are the Adobe online tools really free?', answer: 'Some tools are free to try, and Adobe requires sign-in to keep results; continued use of many tools needs an Acrobat subscription. HatePDF’s tools are free without limits because the processing happens on your device.' },
    { question: 'Can HatePDF fill and sign a form like Fill & Sign?', answer: 'Yes: the Forms tool fills fields and can flatten the answers permanently, and the Sign tool draws, types or places a visible signature. What it does not do is create a certified digital signature — that needs a certificate authority and a timestamp service.' },
    { question: 'Where do my files go with HatePDF?', answer: 'Nowhere. The file is read into browser memory, the operation runs on your device, and the result is saved locally. The completion receipt reports 0 document bytes sent.' },
